  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Fixed\n\n- `KeepAttributedValueBindingOnSingleLine`: when relocating the attribute list from above `let` to inline after `let`, the attribute node's leading trivia (e.g. blank line below a doc comment) is now stripped instead of being emitted in the new position. Without this, the output became `let/n/n[<Literal>] X = …` which is invalid F#. Added a `genOnelinerAttributesWithoutTrivia` helper used only on this code path; the `and`-binding case keeps using `genOnelinerAttributes` since it has no source trivia to lose. Modified file: `src/Fantomas.Core/CodePrinter.fs`. Regression test in `KeepAttributedValueBindingOnSingleLineTests.fs`.",
